 orientation). Stress resilience unknown.\n\nWe could argue that stress resilience is critical for long-distance flights, and we have direct evidence for B, while C lacks evidence. Therefore B may be safer. Also B's conscientiousness indicates reliability. While C's leadership is good, the feedback issue could be problematic in cockpit.\n\nThus we could change vote to B, citing these points.\n\nWe must reference prior discussion: agree that C strong technically, but raise concern about unknown stress resilience and feedback orientation, and propose B as better overall.\n\nLet's craft public message: \"I appreciate the points about C, but I am less convinced because we lack evidence of stress resilience, which is essential. Candidate B has proven stress handling, is very conscientious, and good at weather assessment, which is crucial for long-distance. While B has communication tone issues, they may be mitigated compared to C's poor feedback orientation. Therefore I shift my provisional recommendation to Candidate B.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B handles stress very well; B very conscientious; B good at assessing weather conditions; B sometimes adopts wrong tone; C sometimes not good at taking criticism; C can anticipate dangerous situations (strength). Use these.\n\nNow produce output with PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON vote B."}
